mples\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Thucydides wrote the History of the Peloponnesian War, an account of the conflict between Athens and Sparta that became a model for analytical historical writing.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-78cd-bcc6-2ce40043815f","description":"Thucydides","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-787b-b360-8c7e0e4c0e99","description":"Baruch Spinoza","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-7395-afbf-543c8bdc1b8f","description":"Heraclitus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-791d-87fe-47915f9450be","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-7cf4-845f-c0b7d177412f","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What was pilates originally known as?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Joseph Pilates called his method Contrology, a name reflecting its emphasis on conscious command of the body.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-770c-b3e3-36f3640e1bac","description":"Contrology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-798d-965d-3ef95518a89c","description":"Yoga","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-7837-8486-f5bb135d3eae","description":"The Tibet Method","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-7b3b-8ff8-7dfff079ec46","description":"Balance Therapy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-7440-9f30-1dfb30f5bc90","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name given to traditional Japanese dolls with no arms or legs?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Kokeshi are traditionally turned from wood and painted with simple facial features; they are especially associated with Japan\u2019s Tohoku region.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-7cb4-84ec-202935b52a0c","description":"Kokeshi","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-7fc0-a900-5373ac826caa","description":"Kabuki","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-70e5-94eb-1461cb047e8e","description":"Karaoki","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9a-7442-85f6-02b