rant ruled the Greek island of Samos in the 6th century BC?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Polycrates seized power on Samos around 540 BC and built a powerful navy before being killed by a Persian satrap.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7de0-886f-e6ad4afbac16","description":"Polycrates","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-78ab-8e3a-492b9dbe3aa6","description":"Pericles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7a52-94ff-82b2db3bc4ac","description":"Pisistratus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7a66-ad77-64aeb56c55a6","description":"Solon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-72fe-9895-95928b5bf56a","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Prior to 1941, which language was traditionally written in a Gothic style called \'Fraktur\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"German was widely printed in Fraktur, though the typeface was not exclusive to it. In 1941, Nazi authorities ordered a shift away from Fraktur to Roman type.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7020-8ab2-02a86529f1ff","description":"German","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7b98-83f7-fb37288afa62","description":"Turkish","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-71a4-9416-c32294548ed5","description":"Russian","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7d0a-8358-ba2b6e7aafd9","description":"Italian","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7b7a-9e9d-22d2c421a796","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which influential Queen of Castille helped create a powerful and unified state of Spain, whose influence spread to the Americas?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Queen Isabella I and Ferdinand supported Columbus\'s 1492 voyage across the Atlantic, opening the way for Spain\'s expansion in the Americas.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7a5a-966d-63dd22608312","description":"Queen Isabella I","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-77af-bb40-88b35c1c7c53","description":"Queen Eleanor II","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7925-aa83-f43e678e99e4","description":"Queen Margot III","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7d60-8a9d-b1b8570a4b49","description":"Queen Sera IV","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7566-bc9e-08f0236a4a51","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In Greek mythology, which nymphs tended the garden of golden apples that Heracles was sent to fetch?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Hesperides guarded the golden apples; stealing them was one of Heracles\' twelve labours.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-70ac-8cec-9e8963807b32","description":"The Hesperides","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7ef3-ba90-f131ebd8ed4e","description":"The Gorgons","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7a87-b275-6a3a07f87d4c","description":"The Furies","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7aec-a140-f3033fb02f74","description":"The Muses","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-754a-bc80-d9e605594ee1","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Whose name did God change to Israel?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Jacob receives the name Israel after wrestling with a divine figure at Peniel, according to Genesis.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7522-ab51-73c76c7fe191","description":"Jacob","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7344-bc13-8c3b46b54bc4","description":"Joshua","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7009-8f4d-028f302115b0","description":"Aaron","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7979-9f28-7ed76d585abd","description":"Michael","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7d62-9b8a-22aa5a04a587","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who is the Norse god of poetry?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bragi is the Norse god of poetry and the husband of Idunn, who guards the apples that keep the gods youthful.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7129-965b-8c8bc68d8870","description":"Bragi","correct_answer":true},{