sings.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7f61-a841-b1c5900754a4","description":"Amen","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-72ee-8c8b-9e8875636ad3","description":"End","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-71ca-87e6-4f30a9326fb1","description":"Hallelujah","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7469-a5e4-cb5613b18884","description":"Beyond","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7702-911d-7b427607d002","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which influential theoretical physicist was one of the pioneers of Quantum mechanics?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Werner Heisenberg helped develop matrix mechanics, one of the earliest formulations of quantum mechanics.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7547-a915-f41b4f6d6274","description":"Werner Heisenberg","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7368-b6f8-f48613fa856e","description":"Stephen Hawking","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7cc3-9a36-34a04571ffd8","description":"Gregor Mendel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7d68-8978-592e9cbad7f8","description":"Leonhard Euler","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-70b9-a573-7c5e7dc3d6fd","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which murder-mystery board game was devised by English musician Anthony Pratt during the Second World War?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Cluedo\'s British release was delayed until 1949 by postwar shortages.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-76f4-bcf7-9ea52e5e84e3","description":"Cluedo","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7357-a83a-2c416d957cd5","description":"Mouse Trap","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7544-9fc7-1c5d8225735a","description":"Guess Who?","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7eed-a232-11da77741849","description":"Battleship","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-700e-ba5d-6b902a2a3d49","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who is the mother of Apollo and Artemis?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Leto was a Titaness and the mother of the twins she had with Zeus. Their birth on Delos is a well-known episode in Greek mythology.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-75e0-92ea-bf7901fdb894","description":"Leto","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-71a4-a3b9-cba054ab992b","description":"Diana","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-738a-9e7c-88bc78847534","description":"Helen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-729c-8400-653e9cd693b2","description":"Aphrodite","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-78a6-92b8-6e88a483fab7","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Pig Latin word is used to reject or cancel a statement?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ixnay comes from \u201cnix,\u201d an informal word meaning to reject or prohibit; Pig Latin moves the opening consonant sound to the end and adds \u201cay.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7d74-b417-3d1c78fd9741","description":"Ixnay","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7945-bdd0-3eb5849be5e6","description":"Epay","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-72e6-b4e7-3bfbb46b27a4","description":"Ocklay","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7d25-a643-28f894a271bf","description":"Oopstay","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-78ef-9bfb-8b54dccc3195","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Greek god invented the shepherd\'s flute and had a musical contest with Apollo?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Pan\u2019s reed pipes are commonly called panpipes. In the musical contest, Apollo played the lyre.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-719c-b5d9-0497bba4de98","description":"Pan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7693-b5a6-44afc760c68b","description":"Zeus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7677-9907-bf22565ef483","description":"Artemis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7e73-ae16-efec47b19271","description":"Athena","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7cbe-b767-b581fc43d75b","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who made reading and writing in the Cherokee language possible by creating a syllabary for it?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Sequoyah was a Cherokee silversmith whose syllabary helped literacy spread among Cherokee speakers.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-77ff-b88e-772b6f63bd6f","description":"Sequoyah","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7eab-850f-cf002c599e71","description":"Geronimo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-77ac-811c-46a7f914d182","description":"Sacagawea","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7996-b5ad-73268833c7c4","description":"Sitting Bull","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7926-a51f-12a538f57e4c","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which is not one of the names of Allah?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ar-Brahma refers to Brahma, a creator deity in Hinduism; the other names are among the names of Allah.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7b1b-8eb6-9fdec2e43867","description":"Ar-Brahma","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7222-aaa4-44e848153940","description":"Ar-Rahman","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7b9b-abc3-3a5de3e2ef6a","description":"Al-Malik","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7379-9411-3a2f5f6d294d","description":"Al-Khaliq","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-710f-9d2e-df93efc1d6ba","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In which country do they eat 12 grapes as the clock strikes midnight (one each time the clock chimes) on New Year\'s Eve?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"In Spain, the custom is called las doce uvas de la suerte, or \u201cthe twelve grapes of luck\u201d; each grape is traditionally linked to good fortune for one month of the coming year.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-764a-93ac-c62f8f19dc74","description":"Spain","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7784-8c6d-a90cde3bd9d7","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7370-ace0-ee2423a7540e","description":"France","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7f1c-98d1-7c37cbef5044","description":"Chile","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7c67-bffd-8eec4df29766","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following fashion designers is famous for their use of the color black?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Yohji Yamamoto\u2019s loose, sculptural designs helped shape the look of Japanese avant-garde fashion on international runways.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-71a5-8245-846f203feccf","description":"Yohji Yamamoto","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-72fd-8aac-5bad82d34091","description":"Miu Miu","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7aff-a6bc-e240db117dfa","description":"Dior","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-76e7-94c7-3f39386161a6","description":"Felix Malikovich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-709a-b0c9-67aa8925766e","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who is the Greek muse of dance and choral song?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Terpsichore is often shown with a lyre, and her name gave rise to \u201cterpsichorean,\u201d meaning related to dancing.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-769d-a619-d4f503552865","description":"Terpsichore","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7a52-85df-7d2517b138f9","description":"Penelope","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-75fa-8db0-9670e1077474","description":"Thalia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-70dc-bfc1-f43f45e08e2f","description":"Medea","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7e8d-8f1d-f24cdd38a239","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In which country is the Samuel Griffith Society headquartered, dedicated to upholding the constitution of said nation?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Samuel Griffith was a leading architect of Australia\'s Constitution and served as the first Chief Justice of the High Court of Australia; the society takes its name from him.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7a06-8cc9-6f1d43d2af23","description":"Australia","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7587-beb7-4561edb2f4ff","description":"Canada","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7bc8-a9cb-860bb92c3d61","description":"The Republic of Ireland","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-71e4-ab1e-3032b73e4e88","description":"United States","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7799-a851-11eb831969e5","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What word is used for Germany\'s main highways?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Although famous for unrestricted speeds, many Autobahn sections have posted limits; 130 km\/h is recommended where no limit is posted.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-73bf-92bf-b3d056896b05","description":"Autobahn","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-716e-a94b-4ae6dca9e006","description":"Bundestrasse","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7cb9-8fe7-d814a8cc6eea","description":"Reichstag","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7d58-adf1-15dd3af31473","description":"Schwartzkopf","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7c70-9fd2-c7e26756c55c","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these is a form of clothing worn by women in Malaysia and Indonesia?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Kebaya styles vary across Indonesia and Malaysia, and versions are also worn in neighboring Southeast Asian communities.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-73c5-8e10-341a1e3edb29","description":"Kebaya","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7586-aaed-65eb1b3f3864","description":"Kaftan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-7ea3-bba8-f3941ffd197e","description":"Dashiki","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9b-74de-bb3c-61c1c865c0c4","description":"Thobe","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a