answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7001-8bd2-d5d11963078e","description":"Humiliation breeds subservience","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-70fe-8923-462913497ae6","description":"Humble is the child","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7173-8811-bde7bbe02fa5","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the meaning of the Latin phrase \'Dum vita est, spes est\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\'Dum vita est, spes est\' is a Latin proverb meaning while there is life there is hope.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-706c-961b-44349a6df9bf","description":"While there is life there is hope","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f21-b307-2f0026cb8188","description":"Wisdom is power","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7675-b8cb-631eca09cb53","description":"Every man is the maker of his own fortune","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7d84-9c0c-fe383a69126d","description":"So it begins","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-70b0-a666-48432fa4c92a","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Entities should not be multiplied unnecessarily\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"William of Ockham is associated with the principle commonly called Occam\u2019s razor, a rule of thumb for avoiding unnecessary assumptions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7e26-a940-77423889c26c","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-71d4-aef2-30c2bf51e198","description":"Denis Diderot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-74aa-80e9-56bac6463bb2","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7dca-9da0-758df2c978a8","description":"Spinoza","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7367-b946-76d0a0dfcffa","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Even while they teach, men learn\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Seneca the Younger was a Roman statesman as well as a philosopher; his moral essays and letters remain among his best-known works.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7358-9911-4cad01b5cbc6","description":"Seneca the Younger","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7575-a8cd-d1b2a5fd52ef","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-716c-8ba3-67eb95c1dcaa","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7df5-be55-cfc951dfbf61","description":"Socrates","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7579-8877-10267c9eb23c","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who was the ancient Egyptian goddess of the sky and queen of heaven ?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Hathor was worshipped as a sky goddess and known as the Lady of Heaven. She was also associated with love, music, and motherhood.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7c3b-8d87-a69339e68094","description":"Hathor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-72a6-a9d6-a68b0ff392e4","description":"Isis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-75e9-9a75-881972ff41fc","description":"Set","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7c32-ada8-bee4240652a5","description":"Horus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-719f-bede-2b472923a855","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is a wide cuff that is folded back and fastened with a cuff link called?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"French cuffs are traditionally considered more formal than button-fastened cuffs and use separate cuff links rather than sewn-on buttons.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7ad6-9600-c4f3b51775cf","description":"A French cuff","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7a02-815a-2e81c4b83049","description":"A button cuff","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7d9c-ab67-10f7cc979ad7","description":"A barrel cuff","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-759b-abe2-da93e20efabc","description":"A saville cuff","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-744a-aa6b-709d8abcda03","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'What is rational is actual and what is actual is rational\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The line appears in the preface to Hegel\u2019s Philosophy of Right, where he explored the relationship between reason and the world.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7639-8acd-64e89b547028","description":"G. W. F. Hegel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7617-9d7f-36be9518e223","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7999-a6e0-f1f65fdc057e","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7ad9-bcc1-ae76375d6d06","description":"Democritus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f3e-908f-ee9a682738cf","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In 1982, which member of the British royal family gave birth to Prince William?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Princess Diana and Charles also had a younger son, Prince Harry, born in 1984.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-72f8-a9fb-452bdade26e7","description":"Princess Diana","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-776f-9df6-ec0b3df63161","description":"Queen Elizabeth II","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7306-921b-7534a5703818","description":"Camilla Parker Bowles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-736f-8954-7e8574cb4cec","description":"Sarah Ferguson","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7eba-b6a3-c929a8a63a7c","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Berber is a language spoken in which of these countries?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Berber languages are also known as Amazigh, and Morocco recognizes Tamazight as an official language.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7ace-a989-874d524d17c2","description":"Morocco","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7168-ba2e-942cff0d4428","description":"Kenya","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-767d-9b94-5fd999bf9b07","description":"Tanzania","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7b28-a6b7-014bbd7fd9ab","description":"Sri Lanka","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-71b1-851e-6712fc455fff","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Whereof one cannot speak, thereof one must be silent\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ludwig Wittgenstein\u2019s Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus explores the limits of language and thought.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-70f3-b290-34365403e35c","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-77c1-bada-95a922e3f5a4","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7ad3-8ba4-5b05386a9e6f","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-76e1-94cf-60a4f3e9c1d8","description":"Immanuel Kant","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7953-8f22-21718eb033fe","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Overcome evil with good\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bono malum superate uses a plural command form, addressing more than one person, and echoes the injunction in Romans 12:21.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-787e-a5dc-2634c2aee6d8","description":"Bono malum superate","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7bbc-8e20-8df62519b85e","description":"Bona fide","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7eb4-9787-52992b297332","description":"Humilitas occidit superbiam","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7cb9-9ae3-a5f8c6f79524","description":"Fortiter et fideliter","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7964-8610-e66c7d98a5ad","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'There is only one thing a philosopher can be relied upon to do, and that is to contradict other philosophers\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"William James was also a pioneering psychologist. His work helped shape pragmatism, which evaluates ideas partly by their practical consequences.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7914-9230-08c550a09326","description":"William James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-729c-8bce-0040e6ee2a7d","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7dbb-aaa4-d0bd4764183e","description":"Socrates","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-76bd-86a9-456afbf48690","description":"Martin Heidegger","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7512-ba78-da2c2228e0ec","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the shortest verse in the Bible?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Jesus wept is John 11:35, which describes Jesus mourning at Lazarus\u2019s tomb. It is commonly cited as the shortest verse in English-language Bibles.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f6d-babe-0ba64f870757","description":"Jesus wept","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7471-81c5-e3a36b8dd8a2","description":"God spoke","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7041-9eab-6906870baad5","description":"No more","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7afe-9bef-78444eff5e72","description":"Hallelujah","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f5b-af7d-6046756a7440","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In 2002, which US city saw a number of coordinated sniper killings?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The 2002 Beltway sniper attacks took place across the Washington metropolitan area, including suburbs in Maryland and Virginia.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7160-a4b3-90fe99b89e6d","description":"Washington, D.C.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-73cc-a4e8-0adbc9ade33d","description":"New York City","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7472-8536-fa14442ae541","description":"Los Angeles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-71d4-8cee-0512a879559c","description":"Chicago","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7067-8403-39a26c34b37f","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Pax vobiscum\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\u201cPeace be with you\u201d is a traditional Christian liturgical greeting, often used during worship.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-76e7-9a43-c0917d9fde62","description":"Peace be with you","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7578-ace9-ee352d1a1ec8","description":"In good faith","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f68-9896-a9b90882f5ee","description":"And you, Brutus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7b28-9afa-46e340aea3a4","description":"Nothing is arduous for the willing","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-74a7-98d1-017ae45340c3","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Tempora mutantur et nos mutamur in illis\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\'Tempora mutantur, et nos mutamur in illis\' means times change and we change with them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-71f7-b978-679580b2cc7d","description":"The times are changing, and we change with them","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7180-bf21-a13eb49fbc0c","description":"What is said is done","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-75c7-a310-2344622ab23f","description":"The act done by me against my will is not my act","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7858-b4f0-9fcc6dba7685","description":"Fortune favors the bold","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7c83-81fe-a5033b550af4","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the national animal of Scotland?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The unicorn appears as a supporter on Scotland\u2019s royal coat of arms, often shown chained because it was regarded as wild and untamable.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7017-8d97-183b57051170","description":"Unicorn","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-79bd-8692-bc0351ea558d","description":"Lion","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-74cc-9c0f-3ea491abe3b5","description":"Dragon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7808-9f1b-5a48eadb302f","description":"Horse","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7ef8-905a-f7fa5613d7f8","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What charity organization works to protect the rights of indigenous and tribal peoples?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Survival International campaigns against the forced displacement of Indigenous peoples and defends their rights to their lands and ways of life.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7d27-a58a-b45753277170","description":"Survival International","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-780c-b1d8-92257d1f8067","description":"Greenpeace","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-70f1-95f9-b5067d43dba4","description":"Amnesty International","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f40-9112-c79df522a6da","description":"The Nature Conservancy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7132-a8d3-f431538dd9e9","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'It is undesirable to believe a proposition when there is no ground whatever for supposing it true\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bertrand Russell received the Nobel Prize in Literature for his varied writings, which championed humanitarian ideals and freedom of thought.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7574-ad08-24d417788ed4","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-71ba-986e-f4420066ec5f","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7eab-8b18-722a0f7aa15c","description":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7a1b-9821-371cd2c79f46","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7c4f-b242-8afe8419f354","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Norse god acts as the watchman of the gods, guarding the rainbow bridge Bifr\u00f6st?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Heimdall is also described as having exceptionally sharp senses; some accounts say he can hear grass growing.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-79c6-8ffc-5bd6e7cd00bc","description":"Heimdall","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7b62-94b2-047f96134358","description":"Thor","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7a4c-a60c-06ed553d5ff2","description":"Baldur","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-79d5-9dc0-15778f25c61f","description":"Tyr","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7170-8710-54ebb3864f1e","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'God is not willing to do everything, and thus take away our free will and that share of glory which belongs to us\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Niccolo Machiavelli discusses the balance between fortune and human agency in The Prince, where this line appears.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7a62-b0b4-ce163d4d8ea2","description":"Niccolo Machiavelli","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7118-ae15-9136ec71e0f5","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-71ff-8a59-3808307815a7","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7287-b884-1b4fbe1576ca","description":"Karl Marx","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7bae-9329-d8af312fa72f","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Wisdom is power\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"In Sapientia potentia est, sapientia is the subject, potentia means power, and est is the verb meaning \u201cis.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7c3e-a97c-90649f12f2b6","description":"Sapientia potentia est","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7c72-9578-e4f536e05e2a","description":"Hodie mihi, cras tibi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7c10-a94c-3e53384e7483","description":"Ego te provoco","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7620-a98f-3f394b96d815","description":"Melita, domi adsum","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7341-8cc0-ed5d90cd1794","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following describes John Dalton?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"John Dalton proposed that matter is made of indivisible atoms, with each element having its own type. His ideas helped lay the groundwork for modern chemistry.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7454-894a-868b416a26e4","description":"Chemist and physicist who ade contributions to atomic theory.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-75e4-a77c-2a5a962be4d5","description":"Industrialist who revolutionised mass-production techniques.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7c8d-b14e-c1eeeb1dafba","description":"Confirmed the theory that Earth revolves around The Sun.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7854-8d9b-0dc996f81ce9","description":"38th President of the US.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7e56-859b-289ac67a8402","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the flag flown on a short pole at the bow of a ship?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A jack is flown at the bow, while a ship\u2019s ensign is generally flown at the stern; a burgee commonly identifies a yacht club.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-79e1-bc62-a01e341ab897","description":"Jack","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7530-a942-282d8fda2b68","description":"Ensign","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7e55-9ae0-7490ff3ed1f1","description":"Pennant","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7bc3-82f0-68e8551350a1","description":"Burgee","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-757f-be5b-6bd112c6c150","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Actus me invito factus non est meus actus\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The phrase means \u201cThe act done by me against my will is not my act,\u201d expressing the legal principle that criminal responsibility generally requires voluntary conduct.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-75af-8d57-488677ca7993","description":"The act done by me against my will is not my act","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7b74-aeb1-2be014599481","description":"To act accidentally is not to act at all","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7670-8f3d-6507983ae1e9","description":"Act as if you are always being watched","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-721b-9b7e-63a98321c822","description":"The act of an honest man cannot be questioned","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7966-bee8-37d9a706f2bf","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the US Military\'s highest award for valor in combat?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Medal of Honor is the nation\u2019s highest military decoration, reserved for conspicuous gallantry and intrepidity at risk of life, above and beyond the call of duty.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7c27-bd34-ff2a420b718c","description":"Medal of Honor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-774d-914e-44580cb83a86","description":"Purple Heart","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7950-9ba4-ab77e3625451","description":"Bronze Star","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7a61-8790-6265dbd28900","description":"Silver Star","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7d68-83ac-3bea5579bba6","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'We live in the best of all possible worlds\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Leibniz argued that a perfect God would create the best possible world among all possible worlds. Voltaire later satirized that optimism in Candide.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7870-8da5-c01e382acbf0","description":"Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7e83-95b7-fd5ab67cae6b","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-71f0-9200-c772d40d3cb0","description":"Denis Diderot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7d31-bb01-4092e4d5ac9c","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7802-b461-2776ce99569e","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the first month of the year in the Islamic calendar?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Muharram is one of four sacred months in Islam. Its name is commonly understood to mean \u201cforbidden,\u201d reflecting a traditional prohibition on warfare during the month.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7a78-a168-4de0b976bc07","description":"Muharram","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7782-9f19-68da3dc93663","description":"Ramadan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-766e-b541-69398b41f6bc","description":"Shawwal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7df4-8585-48cd26a5b24c","description":"Jumada Al-Awwal","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7792-823d-771d3e315141","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which country had its first female prime minister, Kim Campbell, serve in 1993?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Canada\u2019s Kim Campbell served for only 132 days before the Progressive Conservatives lost the 1993 federal election.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-731d-9340-e878eb2d46e5","description":"Canada","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7cb4-bf1e-7ae9811842d5","description":"United States","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-75e7-b996-f30a04a515e5","description":"United Kingdom","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7d80-b0bc-65d293574701","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false}]},{"i