ian","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-74bf-95c6-f6e777542579","description":"Dravidian","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f4e-a89d-50411dd5ff14","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"The language \'Sudanese Arabic\' belongs to which language family?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Afroasiatic includes the Semitic branch, which contains Arabic as well as Hebrew and Aramaic.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-705b-a667-cf198c118112","description":"Afroasiatic","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7a0a-b1f9-4a7dd67342a2","description":"Kra\u2013Dai","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-77b0-ac8a-2e097ca837de","description":"Niger\u2013Congo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-73f3-8b1a-bd9a2818979e","description":"Austronesian","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-78f1-8e72-4f0399332aba","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the Hindu scripture that contains the dialogue between Krishna and Arjuna?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Bhagavad Gita is part of the Mahabharata, framed as a conversation just before battle. It is distinct from the Upanishads, the Ramayana, and the Puranas.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7d7a-ad9a-a31e194b5e7b","description":"The Bhagavad Gita","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7556-8b3d-db77f7a62e72","description":"The Upanishads","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7cc3-9bd0-1c84a5bb5bdc","description":"The Ramayana","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-785c-91ea-5f04f7ce9524","description":"The Puranas","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7fe6-8fd2-9cce5466a8a3","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the Islamic call to prayer?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The adhan is the call to prayer recited by the muezzin to summon Muslims.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7628-be53-e98a16ff3270","description":"Adhan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7e5d-a8df-188b9de1b48b","description":"Iqama","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f7c-8793-2a9c92f9b667","description":"Niqab","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7b8e-998b-664baa5e8296","description":"Wudu","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-73f6-8999-919054ddf360","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the Hindu festival of colors?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Holi is also known as the spring festival; many communities light bonfires on the eve of the celebration.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-72dc-ba5a-8b0e2d6b883d","description":"Holi","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-701a-beaf-0663a3844164","description":"Diwali","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7884-beef-0b7d1fef1664","description":"Dusshera","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-735d-8850-876bdc5f9242","description":"Navaratri","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-78ba-9a02-f5cfd8c2a2a9","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Latin music legend is known for her signature fruity hat?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Carmen Miranda was a Brazilian singer and actress who became an international star in Hollywood musicals.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-75d6-b3ce-cbc9593b22e7","description":"Carmen Miranda","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-71e4-aea3-38fbe1cb6402","description":"Gloria Estefan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7b29-83b9-06d844b53cdb","description":"Celia Cruz","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-74cf-aca6-aaff945761d3","description":"Jennifer Lopez","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7d21-ad1f-760f73709478","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Man is born free, but is everywhere in chains\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau opens The Social Contract with this line, setting up his argument about political authority and freedom.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7d65-b567-3daf475b120f","description":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-708a-ac82-bb76eb108a6c","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f2d-a1fc-82a02d13dba5","description":"Spinoza","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7b71-a20b-e17a4db71cfd","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-79cc-b32f-dd3117cb8dc0","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Lead in order to serve, not in order to rule\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Praesis ut prosis ne ut imperes frames leadership as a duty to help others, rather than a license to command.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7b6e-8f92-c51dc31d097c","description":"Praesis ut prosis ne ut imperes","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-78a7-9067-5f830f35dbad","description":"Libertas perfundet omnia luce","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7aae-a2ba-be1f95c96fa2","description":"Non loqui sed facere","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7086-9bfe-6c3615a3eb39","description":"Carpe diem","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-776c-a7c5-16f50568e8aa","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What organisation is based in the Lubjlyanka building?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The FSB is Russia\'s domestic security and counterintelligence agency, and it succeeded the KGB after the Soviet Union dissolved.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7db9-bf63-ef2c4421ed47","description":"The FSB","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7802-b053-d0b7e49cbd3f","description":"The EU","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-713d-8a14-aaa7865854e9","description":"The WHO","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7800-b043-a5b2616878e7","description":"Interpol","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae9c-7f69-a194-ddebadc